WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.040
As you can imagine, with
everything that's unfolded,

00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:05.370
since the senseless
killing of George Floyd,

00:00:05.370 --> 00:00:08.750
we're approaching the show
very differently this week.

00:00:08.750 --> 00:00:11.930
I had a great conversation earlier today

00:00:11.930 --> 00:00:15.830
with W. Kamau Bell,
someone I really respect,

00:00:15.830 --> 00:00:18.320
and I'd like to get right to that,

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:19.970
so without further ado,

00:00:19.970 --> 00:00:23.123
here's my conversation with W. Kamau Bell.

00:00:24.030 --> 00:00:25.300
With what's been going on

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:27.810
in the streets of our
nation over the past week,

00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:29.860
I wanted to have a one-on-one conversation

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:31.700
with a friend of our show,

00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:33.620
who's not only a comedian,

00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:36.470
but a longtime advocate
for racial justice.

00:00:36.470 --> 00:00:40.810
He's the celebrity ambassador
on racial justice for the ACLU

00:00:40.810 --> 00:00:43.870
and he sits on the advisory
boards of organizations

00:00:43.870 --> 00:00:47.660
like DonorsChoose, which raises
money for public schools,

00:00:47.660 --> 00:00:51.140
and Hollaback, an
anti-harassment organization.

00:00:51.140 --> 00:00:54.397
Please welcome the host of
CNN's Emmy Award-winning

00:00:54.397 --> 00:00:58.830
"United Shades of America," W Kamau Bell,

00:00:58.830 --> 00:00:59.740
how are you doing?

00:00:59.740 --> 00:01:02.140
You know everybody asks that question.

00:01:02.140 --> 00:01:03.880
My family's healthy, we're fine,

00:01:03.880 --> 00:01:06.230
but we're also getting
feral with stayin' at home

00:01:06.230 --> 00:01:08.000
and not going to school and stuff.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:11.840
Yeah, yeah, well obviously
I wanted to start...

00:01:13.250 --> 00:01:16.395
We did a show on Monday,

00:01:16.395 --> 00:01:17.228
and I talked to Van Jones,

00:01:17.228 --> 00:01:22.100
and I very much wanted to
make that about listening.

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:26.330
But clearly that's maybe
for me the first step,

00:01:26.330 --> 00:01:29.200
and there's now so much more to be done,

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:30.390
which is...

00:01:31.470 --> 00:01:33.223
I think a lot of us are feeling,

00:01:35.140 --> 00:01:39.430
protests are fine but what can we do?

00:01:39.430 --> 00:01:41.853
And when I say we I mean all of us.

00:01:42.870 --> 00:01:44.300
And people like myself,

00:01:44.300 --> 00:01:48.560
what can we do to make
this situation better

00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:52.370
in a practical pragmatic way?

00:01:52.370 --> 00:01:54.230
Well I mean I think I would, you now,

00:01:54.230 --> 00:01:56.700
first I want to make it
clear that when you say we,

00:01:56.700 --> 00:01:59.168
let's be clear that I
feel like you're saying

00:01:59.168 --> 00:02:00.001
white people as we.

00:02:00.001 --> 00:02:02.470
'Cause I feel like Black
people, brown people,

00:02:02.470 --> 00:02:05.530
people of color, we have
always done this work,

00:02:05.530 --> 00:02:07.240
and we've always had to
figure out what to do,

00:02:07.240 --> 00:02:09.430
in situations where we had very little,

00:02:09.430 --> 00:02:11.470
I mean if you imagine Conan,

00:02:11.470 --> 00:02:13.010
I know it's gonna be hard to imagine.

00:02:13.010 --> 00:02:14.390
Imagine being Harriet Tubman,

00:02:14.390 --> 00:02:16.330
you know what I'm saying like--

00:02:16.330 --> 00:02:17.962
I do that all the time.

00:02:17.962 --> 00:02:18.795
(laughs)

00:02:18.795 --> 00:02:21.100
I know you were up for the movie, but--

00:02:21.100 --> 00:02:23.039
Missed it by that much.

00:02:23.039 --> 00:02:23.872
By that much.

00:02:23.872 --> 00:02:25.670
Harriet Tubman was an enslaved African,

00:02:25.670 --> 00:02:27.960
who had no resources at all,

00:02:27.960 --> 00:02:30.320
and had to imagine what can I do?

00:02:30.320 --> 00:02:32.770
And you know and now
she's in a rightfully so,

00:02:32.770 --> 00:02:34.020
an American Hero,

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:36.549
because in that moment
she just got to work,

00:02:36.549 --> 00:02:38.540
and so I think Black people,
especially Black people,

00:02:38.540 --> 00:02:40.660
have always had to figure out what to do.

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:42.570
So I really put it on white people to go,

00:02:42.570 --> 00:02:44.780
what do you see that you want to do?

00:02:44.780 --> 00:02:47.770
I think a lot of times white
people get caught up in like,

00:02:47.770 --> 00:02:50.080
being scared of doing it wrong,

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:54.630
and I'm like yes be confident
you're gonna do it wrong,

00:02:54.630 --> 00:02:56.200
that's how the work gets done.

00:02:56.200 --> 00:02:58.330
You know MLK and his first move wasn't

00:02:58.330 --> 00:02:59.260
the March on Washington,

00:02:59.260 --> 00:03:01.720
they did a lot of things
to prepare for that.

00:03:01.720 --> 00:03:03.450
You're gonna get it wrong white people,

00:03:03.450 --> 00:03:04.853
get used to doing it wrong.

00:03:05.834 --> 00:03:06.750
You're gonna get do something
you feel good about,

00:03:06.750 --> 00:03:08.875
and then somebody's gonna call you out

00:03:08.875 --> 00:03:09.708
for doing it the wrong way,

00:03:09.708 --> 00:03:11.410
and you're gonna have to get
used to sitting in the space

00:03:11.410 --> 00:03:13.170
of like not doing the work right,

00:03:13.170 --> 00:03:15.630
but right now a lot of white
people are frozen by the,

00:03:15.630 --> 00:03:17.578
I don't know what to
do so I'll do nothing,

00:03:17.578 --> 00:03:21.260
and that's why black people get brutalized

00:03:21.260 --> 00:03:23.510
by police officers, over and over again,

00:03:23.510 --> 00:03:24.690
because white people go,

00:03:24.690 --> 00:03:27.080
"Oh that was so bad I feel so bad,"

00:03:27.080 --> 00:03:30.720
but then a couple weeks later,
"back to my yoga classes,"

00:03:30.720 --> 00:03:33.430
and right now right there's
not going back to yoga classes,

00:03:33.430 --> 00:03:35.340
'cause there's a global
pandemic right now.

00:03:35.340 --> 00:03:36.173
Right.

00:03:37.470 --> 00:03:42.470
There is a sense that right now,

00:03:42.730 --> 00:03:45.660
protests are very visual,

00:03:45.660 --> 00:03:47.850
this is anyway how I'm feeling.

00:03:47.850 --> 00:03:49.553
That you see a lot of people,

00:03:49.553 --> 00:03:52.930
and you especially you
see a lot of celebrities

00:03:52.930 --> 00:03:55.870
being very visual about their protesting

00:03:55.870 --> 00:03:58.563
and then the concern I would think

00:03:58.563 --> 00:03:59.460
and rightfully so would be,

00:03:59.460 --> 00:04:01.850
this is fine maybe in this moment,

00:04:01.850 --> 00:04:04.250
to be visual and to be on the front lines,

00:04:04.250 --> 00:04:08.350
but how are you gonna
follow up on this 3, 6,

00:04:08.350 --> 00:04:11.900
9 weeks from now, next
year the year after that,

00:04:11.900 --> 00:04:14.913
to make America what it should be.

00:04:16.010 --> 00:04:17.780
Well I think that's the important point,

00:04:17.780 --> 00:04:21.280
because even if you Conan
O'Brien go out to a protest,

00:04:21.280 --> 00:04:22.520
you're gonna get a lot of attention,

00:04:22.520 --> 00:04:23.750
people gonna feel that,

00:04:23.750 --> 00:04:26.580
that image is gonna go
viral all over the world,

00:04:26.580 --> 00:04:27.830
you know people are gonna notice it,

00:04:27.830 --> 00:04:30.147
but then Black folks are always like,

00:04:30.147 --> 00:04:31.060
what's Conan doing in his life?

00:04:31.060 --> 00:04:32.643
Right.

00:04:32.643 --> 00:04:33.720
And I think right now,

00:04:33.720 --> 00:04:35.620
it's very important to connect your life

00:04:35.620 --> 00:04:38.580
to the actual movement, and
to the actual making change,

00:04:38.580 --> 00:04:41.610
'cause believe me if you said,

00:04:41.610 --> 00:04:43.941
Black Americans here's what I'm gonna do,

00:04:43.941 --> 00:04:46.720
I'm gonna do a complete
internal audit of my show,

00:04:46.720 --> 00:04:48.910
I'm gonna ask TBS do the same thing,

00:04:48.910 --> 00:04:51.140
of where the Black folks work at TBS,

00:04:51.140 --> 00:04:52.570
where other people of color work,

00:04:52.570 --> 00:04:54.820
and not give you the
percentage of the total,

00:04:54.820 --> 00:04:57.070
but go at what level they are at.

00:04:57.070 --> 00:04:58.810
How many your people are the top level,

00:04:58.810 --> 00:05:01.766
how many people are at the
at the lowest levels at TBS

00:05:01.766 --> 00:05:02.800
and my show.

00:05:02.800 --> 00:05:03.633
And I'm gonna tell you that,

00:05:03.633 --> 00:05:05.330
and then in a year it's
gonna look different,

00:05:05.330 --> 00:05:06.880
and I'm gonna show you
what that looks like.

00:05:06.880 --> 00:05:09.185
I'm gonna tell you about my personal life,

00:05:09.185 --> 00:05:11.070
like in my personal life how
many Black people I interact

00:05:11.070 --> 00:05:11.903
with in my day,

00:05:12.774 --> 00:05:13.850
and in a year I'm gonna work
hard to make that look better

00:05:13.850 --> 00:05:14.683
and I'm gonna...

00:05:15.563 --> 00:05:17.130
Right now we need white
people to show their work.

00:05:17.130 --> 00:05:19.237
You know it's not enough to say

00:05:19.237 --> 00:05:21.160
I'm gonna read Michelle Alexander's book.

00:05:21.160 --> 00:05:23.710
It's enough to go I read it
and here are my thoughts,

00:05:23.710 --> 00:05:26.250
it doesn't anybody have
thoughts about my thoughts.

00:05:26.250 --> 00:05:27.083
I think right now a lot of white people,

00:05:27.083 --> 00:05:30.110
it's easy to sort of like
change your Twitter avi

00:05:30.110 --> 00:05:32.690
to a black background,
or to Black Lives Matter,

00:05:32.690 --> 00:05:34.050
but eventually you're gonna turn it back

00:05:34.050 --> 00:05:36.520
to that wacky picture
you know what I mean?

00:05:36.520 --> 00:05:38.500
So we need white people
to not only do the work,

00:05:38.500 --> 00:05:40.700
but show their work because we can't trust

00:05:40.700 --> 00:05:41.900
that the work's getting done,

00:05:41.900 --> 00:05:43.660
because all these articles are written,

00:05:43.660 --> 00:05:46.355
blogs are written, the
government's done studies,

00:05:46.355 --> 00:05:49.379
the Kerner Commission
released a study that said,

00:05:49.379 --> 00:05:50.280
white supremacy is the rule of the land,

00:05:50.280 --> 00:05:52.010
and this is why these
things are happening,

00:05:52.010 --> 00:05:53.220
but the work doesn't get done.

00:05:53.220 --> 00:05:55.463
We need white people to
show their work right now.

00:05:57.540 --> 00:05:59.440
Something that's occurred to me,

00:05:59.440 --> 00:06:02.120
and I'm sure occurred to a lot of people,

00:06:02.120 --> 00:06:07.120
but money in our society is
a very powerful an engine,

00:06:08.770 --> 00:06:10.780
maybe the most powerful engine,

00:06:10.780 --> 00:06:13.170
where it goes, how it's used.

00:06:13.170 --> 00:06:18.072
And yes there's a lot of rhetoric

00:06:18.072 --> 00:06:19.330
and the rhetoric is very important,

00:06:19.330 --> 00:06:21.653
but sometimes you think,

00:06:23.677 --> 00:06:28.280
how am I helping Black owned businesses,

00:06:28.280 --> 00:06:31.940
how am I employing people of color,

00:06:31.940 --> 00:06:35.530
what are we doing to make
sure that student debt,

00:06:35.530 --> 00:06:38.100
student loan and the price of education

00:06:38.100 --> 00:06:40.500
isn't leaving out a
huge portion of society

00:06:40.500 --> 00:06:41.960
from getting an education.

00:06:41.960 --> 00:06:45.250
What are the practical things
we can do now that last.

00:06:45.250 --> 00:06:46.130
Mm-hmm.

00:06:46.130 --> 00:06:47.536
And--

00:06:47.536 --> 00:06:48.369
I mean there's two different,

00:06:48.369 --> 00:06:49.202
there's two different things.

00:06:49.202 --> 00:06:50.730
There's what can you do that lasts?

00:06:50.730 --> 00:06:52.330
But also what can you do right now?

00:06:52.330 --> 00:06:55.410
There's the house's on
fire, put out the fire,

00:06:55.410 --> 00:06:57.310
and then there's like rebuild the house.

00:06:57.310 --> 00:06:58.720
So I don't want people
to get caught up in like,

00:06:58.720 --> 00:07:00.740
I can give fifty dollars
here, but what can I do?

00:07:00.740 --> 00:07:03.570
Give the money you have
now to support the causes,

00:07:03.570 --> 00:07:05.850
and I'm happy to send
you some causes your way,

00:07:05.850 --> 00:07:07.200
if you don't know what these are,

00:07:07.200 --> 00:07:09.520
but then again it's really about,

00:07:09.520 --> 00:07:11.720
how you are in your personal life,

00:07:11.720 --> 00:07:13.460
cause if your personal life is correct,

00:07:13.460 --> 00:07:15.540
your public life usually is more correct.

00:07:15.540 --> 00:07:17.260
If you are personally invested in this,

00:07:17.260 --> 00:07:18.922
if you're personally like,

00:07:18.922 --> 00:07:19.770
"you know what we don't
have enough Black people

00:07:19.770 --> 00:07:21.310
on this show in high positions,

00:07:21.310 --> 00:07:23.280
so I'm gonna make sure we go
out and find those people,

00:07:23.280 --> 00:07:25.271
and I'm gonna put out a call for this,

00:07:25.271 --> 00:07:28.340
I don't have enough Black
people in my personal life

00:07:28.340 --> 00:07:32.280
that I'm employing or we
are taking advice from,

00:07:32.280 --> 00:07:33.590
I'm gonna change that."

00:07:33.590 --> 00:07:36.840
To me it's like, a lot of
this is focused on outside,

00:07:36.840 --> 00:07:38.210
and it really needs to focus on inside,

00:07:38.210 --> 00:07:39.560
'cause Black people,

00:07:39.560 --> 00:07:42.810
we don't do this work for Black people,

00:07:44.030 --> 00:07:45.903
And one thing white people
need to get is that,

00:07:45.903 --> 00:07:48.950
fighting white supremacy,

00:07:48.950 --> 00:07:51.850
being an anti-racist
should be a selfish act,

00:07:51.850 --> 00:07:53.590
because if the world is more equitable

00:07:53.590 --> 00:07:56.330
and just for Black people,
and people of color,

00:07:56.330 --> 00:07:58.459
it's automatically
better for white people.

00:07:58.459 --> 00:08:01.860
This is truly the rising
tide that lifts all both.

00:08:01.860 --> 00:08:03.860
But I think a lot of
white people feel like,

00:08:03.860 --> 00:08:07.010
I'm doing it for them,
I did this for them,

00:08:07.010 --> 00:08:09.280
I'm done what I'm doing for them.

00:08:09.280 --> 00:08:11.850
And that's why it doesn't,
the work isn't lasting.

00:08:11.850 --> 00:08:12.683
Right.

00:08:12.683 --> 00:08:17.480
I think especially anybody
who has children knows,

00:08:18.450 --> 00:08:22.110
your children and this is for any anybody,

00:08:22.110 --> 00:08:25.420
I mean I think about this a lot,

00:08:25.420 --> 00:08:27.210
I want it to be a fairer world,

00:08:27.210 --> 00:08:28.840
because a fairer and more just world,

00:08:28.840 --> 00:08:31.140
is a safer world for my kids.

00:08:31.140 --> 00:08:32.527
So that is a way to see,

00:08:32.527 --> 00:08:37.527
and if in a very selfish
way, but a very primal way,

00:08:38.060 --> 00:08:41.090
if you're a parent who loves your child,

00:08:41.090 --> 00:08:45.270
I want my child to be
walking around streets

00:08:45.270 --> 00:08:48.410
where the other people
walking those streets feel

00:08:48.410 --> 00:08:50.300
that they have a stake in society.

00:08:50.300 --> 00:08:53.100
Because then my child's safer,

00:08:53.100 --> 00:08:55.010
they're living in a happier world.

00:08:55.010 --> 00:08:57.430
So selfishness is not a bad thing,

00:08:57.430 --> 00:09:00.310
selfishness is very natural,

00:09:00.310 --> 00:09:03.670
and it feels to me that that's--

00:09:03.670 --> 00:09:05.200
I think, I think it is I think it

00:09:05.200 --> 00:09:07.910
I think describing it
selfishness not those two,

00:09:07.910 --> 00:09:08.970
it's helpful to people,

00:09:08.970 --> 00:09:09.840
'cause stop thinking like,

00:09:09.840 --> 00:09:11.800
I'm doing it because I'm a good person.

00:09:11.800 --> 00:09:14.740
As you just said a world that
is more just and equitable,

00:09:14.740 --> 00:09:16.850
is better for your kids,
it's a safer world,

00:09:16.850 --> 00:09:18.433
but it's also a more fun world.

00:09:20.990 --> 00:09:23.440
The best music festivals are the one

00:09:23.440 --> 00:09:24.660
that have all the music there.

00:09:24.660 --> 00:09:26.980
'Cause it's like, we get
to hang out with everybody,

00:09:26.980 --> 00:09:29.140
it's like it's not, it's
not just, a more like

00:09:29.140 --> 00:09:31.440
it's not again we get caught
up in the high mindedness

00:09:31.440 --> 00:09:33.640
of this, get caught up
in the humanity of it.

00:09:33.640 --> 00:09:35.680
Get caught up in the fact that it's just,

00:09:35.680 --> 00:09:39.640
it's a more your children
will be more actualized,

00:09:39.640 --> 00:09:41.470
they'll have more freedom of expression,

00:09:41.470 --> 00:09:43.150
they'll take in more information.

00:09:43.150 --> 00:09:45.130
I mean one of the best
things about being a parent,

00:09:45.130 --> 00:09:46.080
is getting your kids

00:09:46.080 --> 00:09:48.860
to not just eat peanut
butter jelly sandwiches.

00:09:48.860 --> 00:09:50.670
Because that's not a good life,

00:09:50.670 --> 00:09:52.070
that's not a that's not a life

00:09:52.070 --> 00:09:53.430
that leads you down a good direction.

00:09:53.430 --> 00:09:57.400
It's about parents are actively
expanding our kids palates

00:09:57.400 --> 00:09:59.750
but you have to do the same
thing with your kids brain,

00:09:59.750 --> 00:10:01.070
and I'd say I encourage you,

00:10:01.070 --> 00:10:02.885
I don't know how old your kids are.

00:10:02.885 --> 00:10:03.718
How old are your kids?

00:10:03.718 --> 00:10:07.680
I have, my son is 14
and my daughter is 16.

00:10:07.680 --> 00:10:09.670
Okay I mean I think it's important

00:10:09.670 --> 00:10:11.020
to know what they're reading.

00:10:11.020 --> 00:10:13.500
It's important to put both those kids,

00:10:13.500 --> 00:10:15.020
you could put the autobiography

00:10:15.020 --> 00:10:16.500
of Malcolm X right in their hands today

00:10:16.500 --> 00:10:17.740
and they're ready for it.

00:10:17.740 --> 00:10:19.850
You know I think it's important to know,

00:10:19.850 --> 00:10:21.630
to encourage them to
not just read the things

00:10:21.630 --> 00:10:23.200
they wanna read or being assigned,

00:10:23.200 --> 00:10:24.640
but really reach out to other sources.

00:10:24.640 --> 00:10:26.920
That both those kids can
read Ta-Nehisi Coates.

00:10:26.920 --> 00:10:28.590
But then you should read it too,

00:10:28.590 --> 00:10:30.130
and then talk to them about it.

00:10:30.130 --> 00:10:32.220
But with my kids, with
parents of little kids,

00:10:32.220 --> 00:10:35.860
don't - get books that
feature more diverse images.

00:10:35.860 --> 00:10:37.720
I'm a big fan of Mo Willems,

00:10:37.720 --> 00:10:39.610
big fan of Sandra Boynton,

00:10:39.610 --> 00:10:42.280
but also big fan of Selena Alko,

00:10:42.280 --> 00:10:44.980
and big fan of Doc McStuffins

00:10:44.980 --> 00:10:47.109
and other things that
actually reflect the world,

00:10:47.109 --> 00:10:49.333
that my kids can see themselves in.

00:10:51.425 --> 00:10:55.530
There's a lot of talk in
the last two/three days,

00:10:55.530 --> 00:10:59.390
about Black Lives Matter,

00:10:59.390 --> 00:11:02.380
and then some people saying

